     "Methods: The Child Health Study follows a high-risk cohort of 700 children aged 8–13 years, approximately three-quarters with recent state-documented maltreatment investigations. Biennial psychosocial assessments are integrated with multimodal biological phenotyping, including neuroendocrine function, inflammation, epigenetics, genomics, metabolomics, neuroimaging, and biological aging, using advanced statistical and machine-learning approaches.",
