    "abstract": [
     "Introduction: Parental insightfulness, defined as understanding the thoughts and feelings underlying child’s behavior, supports parental sensitivity and secure attachment among neurotypical and autistic children. Positive insightfulness is associated with improved social competence; however, impact on intervention outcomes for autistic children remains unstudied, holding clinical and theoretical significance.",
     "Objectives: We examined the contribution of maternal insightfulness to children’s interactive skills following P-ESDM + community intervention versus community intervention alone. We hypothesized that children of insightful mothers, particularly in P-ESDM, would show greater gains in responsiveness and involvement.",
     "Methods: 82 mother-child dyads recruited from special-education preschools received weekly Multidisciplinary Developmental Intervention (MDI; N=50) or MDI+P-ESDM (N=32) throughout one school year. Maternal insightfulness was assessed at baseline. Children’s responsiveness and involvement with mothers were coded from 10-minute play observations pre- and post-intervention.",
     "Results: A 2×2 ANCOVA controlling for baseline scores revealed a significant Treatment × Insightfulness interaction. In P-ESDM, children of insightful mothers demonstrated significant increases in responsiveness and involvement, whereas children of non-insightful mothers showed no change. Within MDI, children showed no change regardless of maternal insightfulness",
     "Conclusions: Child responsiveness and involvement improved only among children of insightful mothers receiving P-ESDM, suggesting that insightfulness promotes mothers’ engagement and child-attuned interactions. These interactions create opportunities for children to respond and initiate communication more effectively. Maternal insightfulness moderates outcomes in P-ESDM and possibly other parent-mediated interventions, underscoring individual parental differences in intervention effectiveness. Because improvements occurred only in P-ESDM, not in all children of insightful mothers, this reinforces the value of targeted, parent-involved community interventions."
    ]
